.superpowers/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Live pipeline output. Runs write docs/1 … docs/4 and those are transient
# — read them, then clear them. The committed specimen lives outside the
# numbered range, in docs/example-run/, so the iteration cap ignores it.
docs/[0-9]/

# Runtime cursor, written by iteration.py whenever it creates a folder, so
# the write guards can scope by iteration. Transient coordination state, not
# an artifact of a run — it changes on every pipeline step.
docs/.current_iteration

# Mechanical record of hook decisions (see scripts/hook_audit.py). Runtime
# evidence for the live-fire test, not an artifact of a run. The .pre-test
# rotation is written by the runner's preflight (LLM as judge.md, step 0).
docs/hook-audit.log
docs/hook-audit.pre-test.log

# pytest cache
.pytest_cache/
